    "coordinator": "native Squad 2.0.0-preview.4, explicitly adapted for CAO native gh-aw local state"
  },
  "adaptations": [
    "Preserved all actual expert capability detail and 89 casting identities.",
    "Adapted the actual native Squad 2.0.0-preview.4 coordinator for Copilot --agent squad --disable-builtin-mcps with plain local state; preserved name/front matter/version/both original canaries, real specialist delegation, accountable ownership and strict reviewer lockout.",
    "Kept four casting files byte-for-byte unchanged; identity assignment history is required by the registry pair.",
    "Replaced active guidance-only boundaries with explicit CAO one-target admission, dependency gates, independent review and validation.",
    "Removed Azure-only destination mandate; destination is the explicitly reviewed engagement requirement.",
    "Project-owned mission/governance/routing disable automatic monitoring, publication, dispatch and merge; declared CAO safe outputs only.",
    "Replaced source project advisory/skill/tooling links with local lifecycle/contracts.",
    "Adapted Ralph and support policies to bounded on-demand work without weakening evidence or independent review.",
    "Retained 84 upstream specialist routes and enabled the registered execution-orchestrator as the 85th dependency-gated one-target route.",
    "Bundled seven required pinned framework references and three pinned satellite skills. Relocated skills from .squad/templates/skills to .squad/skills; upstream_path records their source locations.",
    "Adapted spawn/completion/model-selection references, response-mode/source-of-truth/reviewer skills, Scribe, Rai and Fact Checker persistence to native host delegation and explicitly admitted serialized local files; no CLI, SDK resolver or state MCP is required.",
    "Removed stale zero-member generated bootstrap, external state/inheritance, init/upgrade/casting, worktree automation, automatic issue/PRD/follow-up and publication/dispatch/merge branches from the actual active coordinator.",
    "Local state does not claim atomic CAS/exclusive-create, transactions or distributed locks. Unexpected writers/uncertain writes stop persistence; source inbox entries remain intact. Optional unpermitted persistence is explicitly not persisted; required evidence still gates completion."
  ],
  "excluded": [
    "engagements and trials",
    "agent histories",
    "customer evidence",
    "learned memories and identity wisdom",
    "source decisions and audit trails",
    "machine-specific configs",
    "MCP launch wrappers/configuration",
    "editor settings",
    "automatic workflows",
    "unrelated runtime templates and skills"
  ],
  "runtime_prerequisites": [
    "Native Copilot gh-aw host with --agent squad --disable-builtin-mcps and actual native specialist delegation plus admitted local file/command tools.",
    "The complete committed team/coordinator/reference/skill bundle materialized together; read bundled skills as files, with no external skill registry requirement.",
    "Explicit native-gh-aw/local config and serialized writers for any explicitly admitted shared local-state paths; no Squad CLI, SDK or state MCP bridge.",
    "Actual CAO workflow admission, tool restrictions, dependency checks and safe outputs outside this asset-only bundle."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Static asset/provenance/reference validation only; no real gh-aw run or end-to-end execution verified.",
    "Explicit native coordinator derivative, not byte-identical upstream or a claim of full framework compatibility; unsupported automatic modes are removed.",
    "Local files offer no atomic CAS/exclusive-create, distributed locks or transactional multi-file guarantee and are not durable across Actions jobs absent declared artifact/safe-output retention.",
    "External state backends, team-root redirection, upstream inheritance, dynamic casting and automatic monitoring/publication/dispatch/merge are unsupported and fail closed.",
    "Host must supply real qualified specialist delegation and independent assurance; unavailable required capabilities block affected work, with no mock runner or coordinator impersonation.",
    "Project constraints are instructions, not a sandbox; real tool restrictions, admission, evidence retention and safe-output enforcement belong to CAO/gh-aw."
  ],
